{"name":"Boxcar","hex":"#873d30","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boxcar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An enclosed railway goods wagon, typically with a sliding door."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reduce to a boxcar function."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boxcar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boxcar","blocks":[{"text":"A boxcar is the North American (AAR) and South Australian Railways term for a railroad car that is enclosed and generally used to carry freight. The boxcar, while not the simplest freight car design, is considered one of the most versatile since it can carry most loads. Boxcars have side sliding doors of varying size and operation, and some include end doors and adjustable bulkheads to load very large items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Box_car.webp/330px-Box_car.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boxcar","wikidata":"Q17102978"},{"title":"Boxcar (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Boxcar were an Australian electronic dance pop group formed in Brisbane in 1986. Their founding mainstay was David Smith on vocals, guitar and keyboards. Three of their singles appeared on the Billboard dance chart top 20, \"Freemason \", \"Insect\" and \"Gas Stop \". They released two albums on Volition Records, Vertigo (1990) and Algorhythm (1994), before disbanding in 1997. They briefly reformed in 2010 and in 2014."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boxcar_(band)","wikidata":"Q4951639"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Box_car_DSSA_18052.jpg/500px-Box_car_DSSA_18052.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Box_car_DSSA_18052.jpg/500px-Box_car_DSSA_18052.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A wooden-bodied Duluth, South Shore and Atlantic Railway boxcar on display at the Mid-Continent Railway Museum in North Freedom, Wisconsin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABox_car_DSSA_18052.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/ANR_Boxcar.jpg/500px-ANR_Boxcar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/ANR_Boxcar.jpg/1280px-ANR_Boxcar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/ANR_Boxcar.jpg/500px-ANR_Boxcar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"ANR Boxcars on a freight travelling through Farragut, Tennessee.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AANR_Boxcar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/GTW_407919.jpg/500px-GTW_407919.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/GTW_407919.jpg/1280px-GTW_407919.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/GTW_407919.jpg/500px-GTW_407919.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A hicube boxcar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGTW_407919.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/NS_488112.jpg/500px-NS_488112.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/NS_488112.jpg/1280px-NS_488112.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/NS_488112.jpg/500px-NS_488112.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An 86 foot long boxcar used for the tra